From: rguisantos <142853894+rguisantos@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 17:55:35 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] xnu: 0150 S21 Ultra (p3s) Wi-Fi: BCM4389 firmware download
 (ARM CA7)

redwood_bcm4375.c (z3sios, fetched by 0142) knows the BCM4375's ARM CR4
with RAM at 0x170000. The p3s BCM4389 C1 has an ARM CA7 and a SYSMEM
core with RAM at 0x200000 (Samsung bcmdhd_101_18). On chip id 0x4389:
find CA7 and SYSMEM, size RAM from SYSMEM banks, download as
dhdpcie_bus_download_state() (BAR1 window 0, CA7 halted, SYSMEM reset;
firmware, NVRAM, seed; refuse a secured reset vector; release CA7), and
load bcm4389-sta.bin / -nvram-semco.txt / -clm.blob. sweet_wifi.c lets
the p3s reach the driver at sweetwifi=4. The BCM4375 path is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BMMeXnUh8SfBzu3GsrA53v
